config BR2_PACKAGE_NVBOOTCTRL
	bool "nvbootctrl"
	help
	  NVIDIA's boot-chain control tool for Jetson (t234), extracted
	  from the nvidia-l4t-tools Debian package. Marks boots
	  successful so the UEFI firmware's per-boot retry counters
	  reset - without this, three boots without a "verify" latch
	  "OS chain A status" to Unbootable and the firmware stops
	  attempting Direct Boot (docs/provisioning.md). Also used for
	  rootfs A/B slot control once firmware redundancy is enabled.

	  Needs /etc/nv_boot_control.conf (shipped in rootfs_overlay,
	  values mirrored from this board's TegraPlatformSpec UEFI
	  variable) and efivarfs mounted.

	  https://repo.download.nvidia.com/jetson/
